# Personal access token for OSF API v2.
# Generate at https://osf.io/settings/tokens (scope: osf.full_read suffices for
# preprint discovery). Required by all scripts in this folder.
#
# Provide it as a shell environment variable:
#
#     export OSF_TOKEN=...
#
# Add the line to ~/.zshrc / ~/.bashrc to survive restarts. Alternatively,
# copy this file to `.env` in this folder (cp .env.example .env) and fill in
# the value — osf_client.py auto-loads a .env sitting beside it (and up to 5
# parent dirs). A real shell env var still takes precedence over .env.
#
# To keep ~/.zshrc as the single source of truth (no secret copy in .env), the
# loader expands a $(...) value at runtime:
#   OSF_TOKEN=$(zsh -c 'source ~/.zshrc >/dev/null 2>&1; printf %s "$OSF_TOKEN"')

OSF_TOKEN=your_token_here
